Now I have a thorough understanding of the entire codebase. Let me produce the comprehensive implementation plan.

---

# Comprehensive Implementation Plan: Samson Tilahun Moges Academic Portfolio Redesign

## Preliminary Audit Findings

**Merge conflict (lines 747–757 of `css/style.css`):** The `main` branch version is correct. It has `avatar-img` (the real `<img>` tag), while the `copilot` branch had `avatar-placeholder` (the old text-initials fallback that no longer exists in the HTML). The correct resolution keeps these four declarations and nothing else:

```
.hero-name { font-size: 1.9rem; }
.avatar-img { width: 120px; height: 120px; }
.btn { padding: 9px 18px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
```

The `about-stats flex-direction: column` and `stat-divider` rules from the `copilot` branch are useful responsive additions but belong in the correct block with `.avatar-img` — they can be re-added as supplemental rules since both sets are actually complementary (the flex-direction column rule was simply missing from main).

**File inventory:**
- `index.html` — 574 lines, all publications inline
- `css/style.css` — 760 lines (759 effective, 1 conflict block)
- `js/main.js` — 85 lines, vanilla JS
- No `favicon.ico`, no `og:image`, no `cv.pdf`
- No `js/` subdirectory scripts other than `main.js`

---

## 1. Recommended Design System

### Color Scheme Decision: Option A — Deep Navy / Teal / Gold

**Recommendation: Option A**, with rationale:

Option C (academicpages white+blue+orange) is already close to the current site. Option B (dark charcoal+cyan) reads as a developer portfolio, not a scientist's. Option A — deep navy base with teal accent and warm gold highlights — is the canonical "credible scientist" palette. It evokes the night sky, aurora phenomena, and the Finnish/Arctic setting of Samson's research. It differentiates from the commodity academic blue while remaining conservative enough for hiring committees at universities.

**Complete Token Set:**

```
Light Mode (default):
--color-bg:             #f7f8fc        (off-white with slight blue cast)
--color-bg-alt:         #eef1f8        (subtle layering)
--color-bg-card:        #ffffff
--color-surface:        rgba(255,255,255,0.72)   (glass cards)

--color-primary:        #0d2b54        (deep navy)
--color-primary-mid:    #1a4480        (mid navy for hover)
--color-primary-light:  #dce8f5
--color-accent:         #0e9e8e        (teal)
--color-accent-light:   #cdf0ec
--color-gold:           #c8952a        (warm gold – used sparingly)
--color-gold-light:     #fdf0d4

--color-text:           #0f1c2e        (near-black navy)
--color-text-muted:     #4a5e78
--color-text-light:     #7a90a8
--color-border:         #d4dce8
--color-border-subtle:  #eaeff6

Dark Mode (data-theme="dark"):
--color-bg:             #08111e
--color-bg-alt:         #0d1a2b
--color-bg-card:        #111f33
--color-surface:        rgba(17,31,51,0.80)
--color-primary:        #4a9edd        (bright sky blue – primary inverts to light in dark)
--color-primary-mid:    #72b8f0
--color-primary-light:  #0d2b54
--color-accent:         #1fcfbc
--color-accent-light:   #0b3d38
--color-gold:           #e8b84b
--color-gold-light:     #2a1f06
--color-text:           #e8eff8
--color-text-muted:     #8aa3bf
--color-text-light:     #5a7a9a
--color-border:         #1e3450
--color-border-subtle:  #152a40
```

Publication quality badges keep their current colors — they are institution-agnostic signals (green Q1, blue Q2) and work well in both modes with minor dark-mode adjustments.

### Typography Pairing

**Replace Inter + Merriweather with:**

- **Display / Name / Section headings:** `Playfair Display` (wght 600, 700) — has academic gravitas, strong letterforms, works at large sizes, used by Nature, Science magazine layouts
- **Body / UI:** `Source Sans 3` (wght 300, 400, 500, 600) — designed by Adobe for scientific/technical reading, wider glyph set than Inter, superior CJK fallback
- **Monospace (DOI links, data labels):** `JetBrains Mono` (wght 400, 500) — cleaner than the default monospace stack for citation counts and year labels

Google Fonts import (single request, `display=swap`):
```
https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:wght@600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@300;400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap
```

### Spacing Scale

```
--space-1:  4px
--space-2:  8px
--space-3:  12px
--space-4:  16px
--space-5:  24px
--space-6:  32px
--space-7:  48px
--space-8:  64px
--space-9:  96px
--space-10: 128px
```

Sections use `--space-9` top/bottom. Cards use `--space-5` padding. Container max-width: `1100px`.

### Border Radius

```
--radius-xs:   4px
--radius-sm:   8px
--radius-md:   14px
--radius-lg:   22px
--radius-xl:   32px
--radius-full: 9999px
```

### Shadow Stack

```
--shadow-xs:  0 1px 2px rgba(13,27,84,0.04)
--shadow-sm:  0 2px 8px rgba(13,43,84,0.07), 0 1px 3px rgba(13,43,84,0.05)
--shadow-md:  0 8px 24px rgba(13,43,84,0.10), 0 2px 8px rgba(13,43,84,0.06)
--shadow-lg:  0 20px 60px rgba(13,43,84,0.14), 0 6px 20px rgba(13,43,84,0.08)
--shadow-glow-teal: 0 0 30px rgba(14,158,142,0.22)
--shadow-glow-navy: 0 8px 32px rgba(13,43,84,0.40)
```

---

## 2. New HTML Structure Outline

The single `index.html` will be restructured. Navigation order and `id` attributes:

```
<html data-theme="light">
<head>
  <!-- Meta: charset, viewport, title, description -->
  <!-- Open Graph / Twitter Card meta -->
  <!-- Favicon links -->
  <!-- Critical CSS (inlined <style> block, ~150 lines) -->
  <!-- Font preconnects -->
  <!-- Font stylesheet -->
