## 4. CSS Architecture Approach

The current single-file approach is correct for a no-build-tool static site. Keep it as one file. The internal structure should be reorganized from top to bottom in this order (with clear comment banners):

```
/* 1. CSS Custom Properties (:root + [data-theme="dark"]) */
/* 2. Reset & Base */
/* 3. Typography Utilities */
/* 4. Layout Utilities (.container, .section, .section-alt) */
/* 5. Buttons */
/* 6. Scroll Progress Bar */
/* 7. Skip Link */
/* 8. Navbar */
/* 9. Hero */
/* 10. About */
/* 11. News */
/* 12. Research / Projects */
/* 13. Timeline / CV */
/* 14. Publications */
/* 15. Contact */
/* 16. Footer */
/* 17. Animations (@keyframes consolidated here) */
/* 18. Accessibility (focus-visible, reduced-motion) */
/* 19. Responsive (mobile-first, ascending breakpoint order: 480, 640, 768, 860, 1100) */
```

**Key CSS principles to apply:**

- All theme-sensitive colors must use CSS variables only — no hardcoded hex values in component rules (the current file has many hardcoded `rgba(29,78,216,...)` values that must be converted to `rgba(var(--color-primary-rgb), ...)` or replaced with token-based approach)
- Glass morphism cards use `backdrop-filter: blur()` with a `@supports` fallback: `@supports not (backdrop-filter: blur(1px)) { .news-card { background: var(--color-bg-card); } }`
- Animation performance: use `transform` and `opacity` only for transitions; avoid animating `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`
- CSS custom property for nav height so all `padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + ...)` references auto-update

